282318,288.611328,232.282318,42.003296,232.084274,291.096252,232.084274,42.003296,221.284302,291.096252,221.284302,42.003296,221.086288,288.578552,221.086258,42.003296,210.286316,288.578552,210.286285,42.003311,210.088272,288.596741,210.088272,42.003311,199.288300,288.596741,199.288300,42.003311,199.090256,66.933350,199.090256,42.003311,188.290283,66.933350,188.290283,51.003311,188.092270,288.606781,188.092270,51.003311,177.292297,288.606781,177.292297,42.003311,177.094254,288.585266,177.094284,42.003311,166.294281,288.585266,166.294312,41.994324,166.096268,288.576141,166.096298,41.994324,155.296295,288.576141,155.296326,41.994308,155.098282,288.581421,155.098282,41.994308,144.298309,288.581421,144.298309,41.994293,144.100266,116.691391,144.100266,41.994293,133.300293,116.691391,133.300293" rect="41.656784,132.962784,291.433777,397.403809" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Given the findings that rugby union can provide health-enhancing&#xD;PA, participants could benefit from a range of associated benefits,&#xD;including a lower risk of developing type-2 diabetes mellitus,&#xD;various forms of cancer,</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.0pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>3 155 156 </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>stroke and heart disease,</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.0pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>3 </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>as well&#xD;as a lower risk of depression.</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.0pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>65 157 158&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>To enable comparison against national and international&#xD;guidelines for PA,</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-8.0pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>10 65 154 </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#0000FF;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>table 4 </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>summarises how rugby union&#xD;may relate to the four PA-related&#xD;domains that comprise these&#xD;guidelines. Further high-quality&#xD;research is required to be able to&#xD;concretely determine rugby union’s exact contributions to these&#xD;PA domains, however, especially in regard to less ‘traditional’&#xD;playing populations across more diverse contexts and countries.&#xD;There is evidence to support a positive relationship between&#xD;both non-contact&#xD;and wheelchair rugby in particular and physical&#xD;health outcomes across a wide range of domains. As such,&#xD;these forms of the game could be actively advocated as health-promoting&#xD;activities across the general population. The evidence&#xD;base is generally mixed or less clear for contact forms of rugby&#xD;union.&#xD;Despite relatively fewer studies, the relationship between&#xD;rugby union and both mental health and well-being&#xD;is generally&#xD;positive, especially in non-professional&#xD;settings. Wheelchair&#xD;rugby in particular has strong wide-ranging&#xD;mental health and&#xD;well-being&#xD;benefits.</span
></p
></body
